                <pb facs="0208" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg862"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in 4 in No.
                    237.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Covarrubias to
                        Mr. Lafragua.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice and Public Instruction</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Section</hi> 1, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 28,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the Citizen Minister of Foreign
                        Affairs, present:</hi></p>
                <p>In a telegram of the 27th instant to this department the judge of the district of
                    the State of Guerrero reports the following:</p>
                <p>“I inform you that last night, at fifteen minutes past eight o’clock, the
                    Evangelical church of this city was attacked by the common people, armed with
                    swords (<hi rendition="#italic">machetes</hi>) <pb facs="0209" n="863"
                        xml:id="pg863"/> and rifles, resulting in five being killed and eleven
                    wounded of both parties, which this court found at the place of the unfortunate
                    event. I learn that there are others in this community. The military commandant
                    and the members of this court hastened at the time to render assistance with the
                    force of the fort. The wounded and dead, among the last an American, were
                    gathered up. The court was engaged during the whole night in the preliminary
                    proceedings. Order has been re-established; no aggressor sound and well has been
                    apprehended. I will communicate whatever occurs.”</p>
                <p>This I transcribe for your information.</p>
                <p>Independence and liberty.</p>
                <closer><signed>J. DIAZ COVARRURIAS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
